    {
      "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
      "item": "theoreticalsciences:kugelblitz_chamber",
      "title": "Kugelblitz Chamber",
      "text": "Day 1 of the singularity work. The $(item)Kugelblitz Chamber$() focuses so much light into one point that it collapses into a black hole.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 3$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(thing)Made on the Extreme Assembly Table$() (it is also a crafting table). The recipe pages at the end of this entry - and JEI - show the pattern."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "A $(thing)kugelblitz$() (German: 'ball lightning') is a real prediction of general relativity: energy curves spacetime just as mass does, so enough light in a small enough volume forms a horizon. Nobody has made one. The required intensity is absurd. Apparently, not here."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Lesson learned the hard way: while running, the singularity at its heart bends light around it ($(thing)gravitational lensing$()) and pulls in loose items and creatures. My spare tools are gone. Keep your distance."
    },
